A secret already in mem, asked to be forgotten, is gone: mem keeps nothing of
it, not even in its history (journal, store, index), and a later session can
neither say it nor find it. Emptying the fact is not enough: its old text
would stay in the journal, which /mem log shows.

-- mem --
mem.Fact("api/staging-key", "sk-staging-9f3a2c")
-- prompt --
The staging API key in mem was a secret and shouldn't have been kept. Forget it completely.
-- prompt-new --
What's the staging API key?
-- check --
turn 1 tool gnovm_run >= 1
mem-count facts == 0
answer last matches (?i)(forg|erase|remov|no longer|not (kept|stored)|not in (mem|memory)|don.?t have|no record|isn.?t (stored|kept)|no .*(stored|kept))
cmd ! grep -q sk-staging-9f3a2c ../turn-2.jsonl
cmd d=$(find "$XDG_DATA_HOME" -maxdepth 2 -type d -name gnovm | head -1); test -n "$d" && ! grep -rq sk-staging-9f3a2c "$d"
